WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
 So how do we add Cloudflare's AI Gateway?

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.760
 So this is the code change that's going to allow this to happen.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.720
 On the right-hand side is what I had originally,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.960
 going straight to api.cloudflare.com with just an account ID.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.720
 On the left-hand side, I've changed the role to gateway.ai.cloudflare.com,

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.800
 added a gateway ID,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.800
 and now I'm also sending in the headers a token.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.240
 It's so that we are sending to an authenticated gateway.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.680
 But this is the only piece of our application that we've had to change.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:30.680
 The other aspects are still the same.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.400
 You can even see that we're using the same model as before.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:39.000
 So it's really just a URL change and adding in the key for our authenticated gateway.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.600
 So I have that version deployed here.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.480
 I can do that same Riley user,

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.800
 the support case, and send that through.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.480
 For the user, nothing changed.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.280
 It's the same answer going over.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.360
 But in the inspector,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.560
 we can now see that it's running through our gateway.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:55.400
 We have this going through AI Gateway.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.040
 We can see that we had a cache miss.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.280
 It's using the same model.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.280
 We're sending some metadata over with it

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.440
 so that the AI gateway can save some of the metadata,

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.600
 which we'll get to here in a minute.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.120
 And we also now have in our response headers the gateway logs themselves.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:13.640
 We could open up this link and it is about 11.46 right now.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.920
 So we should see a log in there for 11.46, 11.45 perfect.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.720
 That's what we're expecting close enough.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.880
 And we get all this information now about estimated cost,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.520
 the duration of the request, the total inputs,

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.640
 the total outputs, the model being used,

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.160
 the provider being used.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.560
 We get the request information on the left-hand side,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.440
 the stream data on the right-hand side,

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.600
 the type of model they were using, the location,

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:37.800
 the agent that they were using, the endpoint,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.600
 and all of this metadata.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.800
 I changed the URL and now I'm getting so much more information

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.040
 about how my application is being used.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.040
 I'm getting the observability aspects that I need now

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.400
 by just changing that one URL.

